WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.710
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna's Part Three.

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.883
We've reached Chapter 15,

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.740
titled "An Investigation into the Nature of Things."

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.450
In Tibetan, here we see

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.130
it called RANG BZHIN BRTAG PA

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:17.560
RANG BZHIN BRTAG PA

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.781
BRTAG PA, meaning PARIKSHA, which means...

00:00:20.781 --> 00:00:21.791
- [Female voice] Research

00:00:21.791 --> 00:00:23.360
- A study.

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.394
RANG BZHIN is an interesting word

00:00:25.394 --> 00:00:28.210
because it means "its own surface."

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:30.055
BZHIN here means surface.

00:00:30.055 --> 00:00:32.330
BZHIN RAS refers to surface.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.060
So RANG BZHIN refers to the
"surface" of something. It

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.040
means nature, meaning... Let's make it

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.710
clear from the beginning, shall we?

00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:46.486
He is referring to the characteristics of things: their inherent nature,

00:00:46.486 --> 00:00:50.012
a certain quality inherent in things.

00:00:50.012 --> 00:00:52.430
So you have to have this feeling...

00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:55.580
We are going to explore, for example,

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.090
whether fire has a characteristic or inherent nature that it

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:04.380
can generate heat, and then this nature will be activated

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.980
and expressed in the world.

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.860
Is the inherent nature of fire heat?

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.900
Then, for some reason, it went viral and spread

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.110
.

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:18.770
Does it have its own unique characteristics?

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:21.130
So when we talk about nature

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:25.820
or self-nature (svabhava) here,
RANG BZHIN, think about it,

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:28.540
this is a thing deep within things,

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:30.080
this is its true nature,

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.160
think about its nature.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:35.700
Okay, now let's look at our argument.

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.250
First passage,

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.629
verse 1.5:

00:01:41.629 --> 00:01:42.987
,RANG BZHIN RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS NI, ,

00:01:42.987 --> 00:01:46.478
'BYUNG BAR RIGS PA MA YIN NO,

00:01:46.478 --> 00:01:48.620
,RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS BYUNG BA YI,

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:51.753
,RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN DU 'GYUR,

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:54.720
If you think carefully,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.820
if the characteristics of something are part of it,

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.758
it doesn't need to be created.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:07.510
If the characteristics of an object are inherent in itself—

00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:10.070
that is, the meaning of characteristics—

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.110
they should not be something

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.131
you only receive when something else happens.

00:02:15.131 --> 00:02:17.075
It must be something you're born with. It's something you're born with

00:02:17.075 --> 00:02:18.160
.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.094
There is no need to heat the fire

00:02:20.094 --> 00:02:22.066
[rubbing hands]. Fire is

00:02:22.066 --> 00:02:23.590
inherently hot.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.950
So if something must be done first to make the

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.583
fire hot, then heat is not the nature of fire. Do you

00:02:31.642 --> 00:02:33.923
agree? - agree. If

00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:36.590
other things need to be done,

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:40.360
if another fire must be lit below the fire to
make it hot,

00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:42.440
then the nature of fire—

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.880
we would not say that heat is the nature of fire.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:48.710
Therefore, we can say that nature or characteristics

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:50.480
come from the things themselves,

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.430
rather than being qualities that only appear when other things exist or when

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:54.000
other causes or conditions exist

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.283
.

00:02:57.283 --> 00:02:59.341
,RANG BZHIN RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS NI,

00:02:59.341 --> 00:03:02.166
,'BYUNG BAR RIGS PA MA YIN NO,

00:03:02.166 --> 00:03:07.100
This is inappropriate.
If the existence of the inherent characteristics of something

00:03:07.100 --> 00:03:09.390
requires the occurrence of other things, there

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:12.090
must be some cause or condition.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:14.040
,RGYU DANG RKYEN LAS GANGS BYUNG BA YI,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.865
,RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN DU 'GYUR,

00:03:16.865 --> 00:03:21.865
Because the nature of what is caused by other factors or causes

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:26.840
is artificial, and the

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:29.856
meaning of artificial is the opposite of that of nature.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:36.070
They were put together and then thrown into the fire.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.480
Oh, come here, let me heat it up for you.
[Rubbing hands together]

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.160
Then the fire gets hot.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:44.450
Then the nature of fire would not
exist in fire itself.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:47.630
It will be artificially created
and then given to fire.

00:03:47.630 --> 00:03:49.934
Okay, do you understand?

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.050
RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.393
Therefore, BYAS PA CAN here refers to something that is

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.850
almost man-made or created.

00:03:58.225 --> 00:04:03.225
In the jewelry industry, there are real
rubies and sapphires,

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:05.783
as well as fakes.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.260
But when people learned to
create real

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:12.980
rubies and sapphires in the laboratory,
there was a great debate about

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.110
whether they should be called artificial stones.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:17.280
Those who succeeded in the process argued that

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.320
it was not man-made, but real.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.020
Another person argued that if it wasn't
dug out of the soil and rocks, then it was

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.690
n't real.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:26.411
So they reached a compromise, which they
called "making rubies". It

00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:32.790
sounds better than artificial products or substitutes.

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:37.410
So this was created,
not natural.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.283
This is the key point.

00:04:40.842 --> 00:04:43.360
RANG BZHIN BYAS PA CAN ZHES BYAR

00:04:43.360 --> 00:04:48.330
If the nature or characteristics of something

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:50.912
must be created from the outside,

00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:52.310
JI LTAR BUR NA RUNG BAR 'GYUR

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.210
Then how can it be said to be nature?

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.740
It is man-made, created. Do you

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.910
understand?

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.410
It's like making a ruby.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:02.800
good.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:04.560
Nagarjuna Bodhisattva...

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:05.970
This is a story.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:08.220
There's a story behind this photo.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:12.273
My Lama, as I have told you,
I served as a volunteer for my teacher for

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:18.300
30 years, and for about 25 of those years

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:23.300
I was his driver,
traveling him between New Jersey and Washington, D.C.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.920
That's a five-hour drive.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.700
He used to teach there once a month.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:32.523
So I've done it over 300 times.

00:05:34.485 --> 00:05:35.730
I told him to go there.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.160
If we count the round trips, there are a total of 600 trips.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:42.430
So I know those routes by heart,
and I really enjoy driving him.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:46.000
Because he always refuses to answer my questions.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.220
He couldn't refuse in the car.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.565
He was locked in the car for five hours,

00:05:52.565 --> 00:05:55.730
and the car he ordered didn't have a radio,

00:05:55.730 --> 00:05:58.707
so I couldn't listen to the radio.

00:05:58.707 --> 00:06:01.667
Ordering a car without a radio
requires an extra fee.

00:06:01.667 --> 00:06:03.069
[Laughter]

00:06:03.069 --> 00:06:06.353
In short, all we can do is discuss Buddhism.

00:06:06.353 --> 00:06:08.655
Sometimes he would pretend to be asleep.

00:06:08.655 --> 00:06:11.367
I would say I know you're not asleep.

00:06:11.367 --> 00:06:13.190
Then he...
[imitates snoring]

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:18.190
Anyway, he always


00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:21.083


00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:23.840
stops at Howard Johnson's restaurant in front of the Delaware Bridge, which is located at the intersection of Maryland and Delaware.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:26.010
We always stopped at the same spot, and he

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.630
would order tea. As

00:06:28.630 --> 00:06:30.110
you know, he loves drinking tea.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.930
He drinks about 15 cups of tea a day

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:36.367
. I make him 15-20 cups of tea a day.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:40.245
They will try to provide him with creamer.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.160
He would say, "No,

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.218
I want cream." "That's creamer, I don't want creamer.

00:06:45.218 --> 00:06:48.460
I want cream, I want the real thing."

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:50.110
He taught me these words:

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.080
artificial, fake, unnatural.

00:06:54.150 --> 00:06:57.570
Everything I learned from him,
including my own use of words, has a

00:06:57.570 --> 00:06:58.870
structure.

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.910
We were sitting somewhere, and he said,

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.285
"This is called BCOS MA."

00:07:03.285 --> 00:07:04.326
BCOS MA stands for BYAS PA.

00:07:04.326 --> 00:07:06.750
BYAS PA means that it must be
created from the outside world.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.240
This is not natural.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.884
good.

00:07:10.884 --> 00:07:13.075
He hates this stuff, he

00:07:13.942 --> 00:07:15.025
really does.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.363
good.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.545
Next paragraph. It is actually only half a section.

00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:25.657
This is actually RANG LUGS.

00:07:25.657 --> 00:07:27.603
What does that mean?

00:07:27.603 --> 00:07:30.069
This is our argument.

00:07:30.069 --> 00:07:32.044
,RANG BZHIN DAG NI BCOS MIN DANG,

00:07:32.044 --> 00:07:34.490
,GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA YIN,

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:38.320
If it is a real characteristic, it

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:40.398
should not be BCOS MA.

00:07:40.398 --> 00:07:43.990
BCOS MA means man-made or
artificial creation. It


00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:46.050
shouldn't taste like creamer. It must

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:48.248
be true.

00:07:48.248 --> 00:07:50.983
BCOS MIN means non-creative.

00:07:50.983 --> 00:07:55.020
What is the famous BCOS PA in the Stages of the Path?

00:07:56.522 --> 00:07:58.640
BCOS MA? It means trying to feel like a Bodhisattva

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:00.206
when you are not yet one

00:08:00.206 --> 00:08:03.060
.
[Laughter]

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.060
That's good, BCOS MA.

00:08:05.060 --> 00:08:07.493
Good. A fake Bodhisattva. The

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:09.920
Bodhisattva created.

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.591
Artificial, you pretend to be a bodhisattva,

00:08:13.591 --> 00:08:16.885
but then you still mess around all day, and things like that.

00:08:16.885 --> 00:08:18.170
,GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA YIN,

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:20.800
If it is the true nature, it

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:23.190
should not need to rely on any

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.360
external conditions to exist.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:28.590
If fire is inherently hot, then it doesn't matter

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:31.280
where the fire is or

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.430
what happens to it.

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.103
He should be warm from the inside out.

00:08:35.103 --> 00:08:36.700
Like this.

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.348
This is our definition of nature.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:44.590
I was thinking, maybe you
could consider it. Is

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:47.468
this BTAGS PA MTHA'
BZUNG GI RIGS PA? Is

00:08:47.468 --> 00:08:49.670
this BTAGS PA MTHA'
BZUNG GI RIGS PA?

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:52.230
This is a very, very useful expression.

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:55.500
I remember once I was debating Buddhist scriptures

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:57.440
at Drepung Monastery.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.740
I heard this statement, BTAGS
PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA.

00:09:01.740 --> 00:09:05.320
BTAGS PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS
PA, means theoretical argument.

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:06.260
Theoretical case studies.

00:09:06.260 --> 00:09:10.350
In theoretical cases, the nature of things

00:09:10.350 --> 00:09:13.917
should possess two qualities. What is it?

00:09:13.917 --> 00:09:16.330
BCOS MIN
should not be a human creation; it

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.050
should be GZHAN LA LTOS PA MED PA.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.450
It should not

00:09:22.441 --> 00:09:24.700
depend on other conditions.

00:09:24.700 --> 00:09:28.620
So, does such an inherent property exist?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.413
This is another debate, you know?

00:09:30.413 --> 00:09:34.221
Theoretically speaking, we said
theoretically, right? Theoretically

00:09:34.221 --> 00:09:36.120
speaking, that's just how it is. Do

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.370
you know if
such a thing actually exists? We don't know.

00:09:40.333 --> 00:09:45.308
Lama Qiuni also expressed his views.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:49.240
This is a very traditional and ancient view

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:52.870
about what nature should be like if it truly exists
, and that it

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.310
should possess three qualities.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:55.730
Ready?

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.171
First.

00:09:58.682 --> 00:09:59.515
GNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:09:59.515 --> 00:10:00.348
GNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:10:01.437 --> 00:10:04.120
GNYUG MA is a very, very rare and

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:09.120
important word, meaning since beginningless time

00:10:09.253 --> 00:10:10.650
[laughter].

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.002
GNYUG MA

00:10:12.002 --> 00:10:12.940
sounds like SMYUG MA,

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:16.016
which means "bamboo shoot," but it doesn't.

00:10:16.016 --> 00:10:18.700
GNYUG MA means original,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:21.961
primitive, from the very beginning.

00:10:21.961 --> 00:10:24.860
GNYUG MAGNYUG MA'I NGO BO

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:29.030
If this is the nature of fire,

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:32.830
then this nature will always exist within fire. Do you

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:33.911
understand?

00:10:33.911 --> 00:10:36.332
It refers to heat, intense heat.

00:10:36.332 --> 00:10:38.380
If...

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:43.380
if fire has an inherent nature, then
that nature or characteristic

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.150
will always exist within those things

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:49.370
as long as fire exists.

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:51.200
That's the first point.

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:53.820
Fire is always hot.

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.753
Second point.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:11:01.680
Whether you're discussing fire a hundred years ago,

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:03.930
fire a hundred years from now,

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.263
or the fire in this room right now,
it should remain unchanged.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:11.420
Features will always exist.

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:14.510
Whether you're talking about fire a hundred years from now,

00:11:14.510 --> 00:11:15.840
fire a hundred years ago,

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:18.003
or fire right now, the

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:21.883
characteristics of fire remain.

00:11:22.850 --> 00:11:24.480
hot.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.513
Third point.

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:31.300
Its properties should not depend on

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:35.190
other sources.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.790
He also gave an interesting example.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:41.398
You don't need to put a kettle on the stove.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:46.100
Veronica and I recently
got something really cool that

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:47.430
someone gave us. Was it a

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:49.913
cherry pit? It

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:53.043
was in a bag?

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:57.360
It also contains lavender flowers.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:12:00.530
Put it in the microwave to heat it up,

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.880
and then lie on it. It's

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:04.220
very comfortable to sleep like this. It will

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:07.529
stay warm for about half an hour, then

00:12:07.529 --> 00:12:10.026
gradually cool down, and you can lie down on it and fall asleep. It

00:12:10.026 --> 00:12:12.601
is very comfortable.

00:12:14.069 --> 00:12:17.180
It looks a bit like a kettle.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:18.463
In short, Lama Qiuni said that

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.208
if the heat of the fire comes from within, there is

00:12:24.208 --> 00:12:26.768
no need to

00:12:26.768 --> 00:12:28.723
heat the fire with a kettle.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:34.520
This is a pillow filled with cherry pits and
lavender.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:37.850
If you don't need to microwave a cherry pit lavender pillow

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.180
to warm yourself up,

00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:44.319
you're probably warmed by nature. Do you

00:12:44.319 --> 00:12:46.053
understand?

00:12:46.053 --> 00:12:47.150
These are the three key elements. Once

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.150
again, this might be BTAGS
PA MTHA' BZUNG GI RIGS PA.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:54.203
In the photo, a woman is about to touch the candlelight.

00:12:55.090 --> 00:12:57.650


00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:00.180
You might say something like, "

00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:02.600
I hope she doesn't put her fingers in the fire

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:04.300
because it will burn her."

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:06.960


00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.723


00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:18.730


00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:24.863
You might automatically think, "I hope she doesn't put her fingers in the fire because it will burn her." Its nature
is to be hot. Okay, next paragraph. These are some other thoughts

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:29.290


00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:31.790


00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:34.822
on the features.

00:13:34.822 --> 00:13:36.196


00:13:36.196 --> 00:13:38.810


00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.415


00:13:43.480 --> 00:13:47.620
You should know that my main ideas about characteristics are those three elements, but let's talk about other things together. Let's talk about other features regarding the concept of characteristics. ,RANG BZHIN YOD PA MA YIN NA, ,GZHAN GYI DNGOS PO GA LA YOD, It is very complicated. If you think about it carefully, fire has two natures.

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:52.093
One originates from within, the other from

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.390


00:13:56.390 --> 00:14:00.523
 
without. For example, the color of fire. "Originating from the outside world" means "

